      "content": "I'll read both the CUT and the original test file to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of both files. Let me write an improved test with better understandability — clearer method names, accurate assertion messages, logical grouping, and explanatory comments where the \"why\" isn't obvious.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `RefinedSoundexTest.java` is ready — key understandability improvements include: renamed the three generic `testNewInstance*` methods to clearly describe which constructor variant they test, fixed the misleading assertion message in `testGetMappingCodeNonLetter`, added class-level and per-method Javadoc explaining the algorithm and what each test verifies, and added inline comments in `testEncode` to make the pangram structure explicit."
